{"model":"claude-opus-5-5-max","id":"msg_proxy_c4856dc47cdf4b3687da49dafe9b9afb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"**Contested.**\n\nSupporters of a breakup argue that a few platforms control search, app stores, ads, and cloud infrastructure, letting them self-preference and squeeze out European rivals. They say structural separation would work better than fines, which these companies treat as a cost of doing business. Opponents argue that breakups would weaken the scale behind services Europeans rely on, and might hand the advantage to Chinese firms rather than European ones. They also note that the Digital Markets Act already gives the EU conduct rules, and say it should be given time to work first. The disagreement comes down to whether rules on behavior can restrain market power, or whether only changes to company structure will."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13956,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2361,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"iterations":[{"input_tokens":13956,"output_tokens":403,"cache_read_input_tokens":2361,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"output_tokens":403,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":189},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":{"applied_edits":[]}}